{"30":[{"k":"p","t":"4."},{"k":"p","t":"5. MOVING THE MACHINE"},{"k":"p","t":"This machine is fitted with castors to make it easier to move. Take care when moving the machine on an inclined surface."},{"k":"p","t":"The overall height of the machine is 2090mm. Take care of any overhead obstructions. (e.g. Light Fittings, Electric Cables etc.)"},{"k":"p","t":"When moving the game, ensure that the game is disassembled into 3 parts: Monitor Assembly, Ride Assembly, and Header Assembly."},{"k":"p","t":"INSTALLATION"},{"k":"p","t":"Notes on Installation"},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   -   NEVER turn the power to the machine ON until"},{"k":"p","t":"installation has been completed."},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   -   In order to prevent possible electric shocks, be sure"},{"k":"p","t":"that the machine is connected to the mains with a securely connected earthed plug."},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   +   So that customers are not injured , ensure that there is"},{"k":"p","t":"at least 500mm separation between other machines or walls."},{"k":"tr","t":"CAUTION   +   In order to avoid damage to the machine due to mis-"},{"k":"p","t":"operation, ensure that the voltage of the mains supply is 230volts AC. )"},{"k":"h","t":"NOTE . If the location site of this machine has a polished floor it is"},{"k":"p","t":"recommended that rubber pads are fitted under the level adjusters to prevent the machine sliding on the floor."},{"k":"p","t":". In order to gain access to the Power Supply and CPU assemblies, make sure that the rear of the machine is separated from a wall or other machine by at least 500mm."},{"k":"p","t":". When installation is complete, it is imperative that the game is initialized. (See section 7 page 56)"}],"43":[{"k":"p","t":"6-2 Adjustment Switches"},{"k":"p","t":"The Adjustment switches are located inside the coin door."},{"k":"p","t":"1. Service Switch. Press this switch to obtain game credits without incrementing the play meter."},{"k":"p","t":"Test Switch Slide the test switch ON to enter test mode. Test mode allows testing and the changing of game settings. (Refer to section 6-3 \"Test Mode\" page 46)"},{"k":"p","t":"Select Up/Down Switch This switch is used to select the test required when in the Test Mode."},{"k":"p","t":"Enter Switch This switch is used to enter a selected test and to change settings within a test."},{"k":"p","t":"COIN COUNTER o 2 Amp Q/B (Coin Fuse) \u00b0 fe)"},{"k":"p","t":"PLAYER 1 PLAYER 2"},{"k":"p","t":"UP UP @| SELECT @| SELECT DOWN DOWN"},{"k":"p","t":"SELECT SELECT"},{"k":"tr","t":"O   \u201c\u00a9   O   \u201coe"},{"k":"tr","t":"TEST   SERVICE   TEST   SERVICE"},{"k":"tr","t":"\u00a9   t   )"}],"46":[{"k":"p","t":"6-3-2 Game Options"},{"k":"li","t":"1. Select \u201cGAME OPTIONS\u201d on the menu screen to set the game variables. The following screen is displayed."},{"k":"li","t":"2. Use the Select Up/Down switch to choose the required item then press the Enter button."},{"k":"li","t":"3. Use the Up/Down switch to change the setting."},{"k":"li","t":"4. Select \u201cEXIT\u201d and press the Enter button to return to the menu screen."},{"k":"p","t":"( >) GAME OPTIONS"},{"k":"p","t":"<DEFAULT IN GREEN>"},{"k":"tr","t":"PCB ID   1   (a)"},{"k":"h","t":"ENTRY WAIT 14 (b)"},{"k":"tr","t":"ATTRACT SOUND   ON   \u2014\u2014\u2014aceeeetteststsesfeteeeeeseseeneee   (c)"},{"k":"p","t":"GAME DIFFICULTY"},{"k":"tr","t":"SPEED   C (MEDIUM)   on. eeeececsseafeceeeeseseeeeee   (d)"},{"k":"tr","t":"TECHNICAL   E (HARD)   viseecsteteteesfeeeeeeeeeeee   (e)"},{"k":"tr","t":"HI-SCORE INIT   NO   seacestseeteseefesesteeeeeseeees   (f)"},{"k":"p","t":"EXIT"},{"k":"p","t":"SELECT SW : CHOOSE ENTER SW : ENTER Ne y,"},{"k":"h","t":"ITEM DESCRIPTION FACTORY SET"},{"k":"tr","t":"(a) PCB ID   Sets PCB number to player number ---- settable 1 - 4   1/2"},{"k":"tr","t":"(c) Attract Sound   Sound in attract mode ON /OFF   ON"},{"k":"tr","t":"(d) Speed Course   A (Very Easy) to E (Very Hard)   B (Easy)"},{"k":"li","t":"(e) Technical Course |A (Very Easy) to E (Very Hard) B (Easy)"},{"k":"tr","t":"(f) Hi-Score Init?   Hi-Score initialized at power up YES/NO   NO"},{"k":"note","t":"Note:"},{"k":"li","t":"(i) PCB ID numbers are assigned so that they are not duplicated on the linked seats. Be sure to set these correctly to avoid link absence or other operation faults. PCB ID numbers (1 ~ 4) are matched to the numbers of the current players (1P ~ 4P)."},{"k":"p","t":"(ii) The same degree of difficulty must be set for all of the linked seats. If different degrees of difficulty are set, the machine will not operate correctly."}],"53":[{"k":"p","t":"6-3-6 ADS Data"},{"k":"p","t":"By selecting ADS Data from the menu screen, all of the bookkeeping details can be read and/or reset."},{"k":"p","t":"6-3-7 Others"},{"k":"li","t":"1. Select \u201cOTHERS\u201d on the menu screen. The following screen is displayed."},{"k":"li","t":"2. Use the Select Up/Down switch choose the required item then press the Enter button."},{"k":"li","t":"3. Select \u201cEXIT\u201d and press the Enter button to return to the menu screen."},{"k":"p","t":"( OTHERS >)"},{"k":"tr","t":"ROM1 Ver.   97/07/07   MON   21:15:59   J (a)"},{"k":"tr","t":"ROM2 Ver.   97/06/27   FRI   20:11:35"},{"k":"tr","t":"CLOCK   97/08/27   WED)   28:11:12   \u2014...... eve"},{"k":"p","t":"PCB TEST VIDEO TEST LANGUAGE ENGLISH BACKUP MEMORY INITIALIZE EXIT"},{"k":"p","t":"S SELECT SW: CHOOSE ENTER SW: ENTER )"},{"k":"p","t":"(a,) Displays game software version."},{"k":"li","t":"(b) Allows the internal clock and calendar to be set."},{"k":"li","t":"(c) Used to test the PCB. (this function is only for factory testing)"},{"k":"li","t":"(d) Sets the language displayed on the screen"},{"k":"li","t":"(e) When selected the Data Initialization Menu appears. To reset all game settings to factory setting and clear all stored data , select YES from the Data Initialization menu then press the Enter button."},{"k":"p","t":"After initializing the backup data ensure that the gam